.\" Manpage for git-subtree-report
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0
.Dd April 17, 2025
.Dt GIT-SUBTREE-REPORT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm git-subtree-report
.Nd Analyze Git repositories/subtrees for safe file concatenation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o
.Op Fl e Ar pattern
.Op Fl r Ar ref
.Op Fl C Ar dir
.Op Fl t Ar path
.Op Fl s Ar size
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility performs deep analysis of Git repository subtrees to determine file safety for concatenation outputs. Key features include:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Full tree visualization with exclusion patterns
.It
Multi-level safety checks (binary detection, encoding validation)
.It
Integration with Git LFS and submodules
.It
Historical analysis at any commit reference
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl C Ar dir
Change working directory before analysis (supports bare repos)
.It Fl e Ar pattern
Exclude paths matching Perl-compatible regular expression
.It Fl o
Enable concatenation output mode (generates combined safe files)
.It Fl r Ar ref
Analyze repository state at specified commit/branch/tag
.It Fl s Ar size
Set maximum filesize for detailed analysis (e.g., 5M, 100K)
.It Fl t Ar path
Subdirectory path to analyze (relative to repo root)
.It Fl -help
Show full help message with examples
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev LC_ALL
Overrides locale settings (requires C.UTF-8)
.It Ev NO_COLOR
Disables colored output when set
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/git-subtree-report
Typical installation path
.It Pa ~/.config/git-subtree-report/cSpell.json
Custom spelling dictionary (optional)
.It Pa examples/initial_commit.txt
Sample report output
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Analyze src/ directory in CI environment:
.Dl $ git-subtree-report -C /build/repo -t src/ -e '\.csv$' -s 2M
.Pp
Generate concatenated output for documentation audit:
.Dl $ git-subtree-report -t docs/ -o | less -R
.Pp
Analyze project state from 3 months ago:
.Dl $ git-subtree-report -r $(git rev-list -n1 --until="3 months ago")
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr perl 1 ,
.Xr numfmt 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Cameron Garnham Aq Mt me@da2ce7.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Special considerations for repository types:
.Bl -bullet
.It
For bare repositories:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Must be invoked from repository root directory, OR
.It
Use
.Fl C Ar /path/to/bare/repo.git
to specify full path to repository root
.El
.It
When combining
.Fl C
and
.Fl t :
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Fl C
must always point to repository root (never subdirectories)
.It
.Fl t Ar path
resolves relative to repository root (not working directory)
.El
.It
All operations prevent upward path traversal (e.g., ../)
.El
